    "result_text": "The build is green. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What I implemented\n\n`membershipTier` now becomes `GOLD` when the owner's household (owners sharing the same `householdId`) has 3+ members after the create; otherwise the existing SILVER/BRONZE rules apply.\n\nFollowing the project's existing `namesakeCount` pattern (a value frozen at create time and persisted onto the owner, from which the mapper derives a read-time field), I:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `GOLD` to the `membershipTier` enum and updated its description (so the generated `OwnerDto.MembershipTierEnum` has `GOLD`).\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `householdSize` field (`household_size` column) with getter/setter.\n\n3. **Schema SQL** (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `household_size INTEGER` column.\n\n4. **`AssignHouseholdSize.java`** (new function) \u2014 runs after `AssignHousehold` and before `SaveOwner`; counts existing owners sharing the new owner's `householdId` plus the owner being created (1 when not in a shared household), and stores it on the owner. Since `AssignHousehold` backfills every existing household member with the shared id before this step, the third member's count comes out as 3.\n\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the `assignHouseholdSize` step into the create pipeline (under `govern: [ transaction ]`, between `assignHousehold` and `save`).\n\n6. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 `toMembershipTier` returns `GOLD` when `householdSize >= 3`, else falls through to the existing SILVER/BRONZE logic; also ignored `householdSize` in the `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` mapping.\n\nBecause the tier derives from the persisted `householdSize`, both the create response and later `GET`s report it consistently, and it reflects the household size \"after this create\" per-owner (matching the spec's wording and the frozen-at-create semantics of the existing `namesakeCount` rule).\n\nThe full test suite (the single `AcceptanceTest`, including the new `coreGoldForThreeMemberHousehold` case) passes: **Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0**.",
